      "principle": "A petition for divorce under the Hindu Marriage Act, 1955 is maintainable only if it is proved that the respondent has been guilty of adultery.",
      "held": "It is held that a petition for divorce under the Hindu Marriage Act, 1955 is maintainable only if it is proved that the respondent has been guilty of adultery. The burden lies on the petitioner to prove this fact beyond reasonable doubt.",
